---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import { sitePath } from "../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About the ARISE research programme website demonstrator and the content still to be agreed."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About the programme"
    title="Assembly and robotics innovation in steel building erection."
    intro="The initial proposal frames ARISE as an interdisciplinary programme exploring intermeshed steel connections, advanced manufacturing, structural performance, robotic assembly and the human dimensions of technology adoption. Public wording remains provisional pending consortium review."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split-layout">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Purpose</p>
        <h2>Bring the programme's connected work into view.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose lead-prose">
        <p>
          A research-programme website needs to answer a few simple questions
          well: what is the programme, who is involved, what research is under
          way, and where can people find the resulting publications and
          resources?
        </p>
        <p>
          This vertical slice shows those answers as structured, reusable
          content. It is a working basis for a consortium conversation about
          official ownership, branding, content approval and long-term
          maintenance.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section
    class="section section--tint"
    aria-labelledby="research-context-heading"
  >
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Research context</p>
        <h2 id="research-context-heading">
          A connected view of future steel assembly.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-grid">
        <article>
          <span class="principle-grid__number">01</span>
          <h3>Connections and manufacture</h3>
          <p>
            Study how intermeshed steel connections can be designed, produced
            and assembled, including the relationship between connection
            geometry and manufacturing processes.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="principle-grid__number">02</span>
          <h3>Robotics and perception</h3>
          <p>
            Explore computer vision, machine learning, simulation and robotic
            manipulation for steel connection assembly.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="principle-grid__number">03</span>
          <h3>Performance, safety and adoption</h3>
          <p>
            Connect structural modelling and physical testing with questions of
            safety, ergonomics, skills, cost and technology adoption.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="verification-note">
        These are research directions distilled from the initial proposal, not
        completed outcomes or the final approved work-package structure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="known-heading">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Evidence boundary</p>
        <h2 id="known-heading">
          What this demonstrator does—and does not—claim
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="principle-grid">
        <article>
          <span class="principle-grid__number">01</span>
          <h3>Supplied context</h3>
          <p>
            ARISE is an international, multi-institutional collaboration, and
            Debra Laefer is identified as overall global lead.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="principle-grid__number">02</span>
          <h3>Visible placeholders</h3>
          <p>
            Unverified biographies, publication data and project detail are
            clearly marked instead of being filled with invented claims.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="principle-grid__number">03</span>
          <h3>Decisions still needed</h3>
          <p>
            Official wording, branding, institutional roles, editorial ownership
            and the permanent domain remain consortium decisions.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell callout-panel">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Explore the model</p>
        <h2>See how one project connects the site.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          ISC-XR is used as a representative project record, with demonstration
          links to people and outputs.
        </p>
        <a class="button" href={sitePath("/research/isc-xr/")}
          >Open the ISC-XR example</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
